  <office:body>
    <office:text>
      <text:p text:style-name="Title">Interior design brief template</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Subtitle">Blank editable template</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">OpenLintel • Educational planning resource • September 27, 2026</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Illustrative teaching extension of The Window Room; not a client record, supplier quote, site survey, or construction-ready document. Pending professional review.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">How to use</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Complete this after discovery, not instead of discovery. Read the objectives back to the client in plain language.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Revisit the brief when scope changes rather than quietly changing its meaning in a presentation. Preserve the agreed brief revision when discussing new needs; review effects on scope separately.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">●　Extract needs and constraints from the questionnaire.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">●　Check each proposed deliverable against the objectives.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">●　Confirm unresolved items and review the brief before starting the next phase.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">Review before use</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">●　Avoid vague aims such as “make it better” without explaining use.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">●　Do not hide exclusions in notes that nobody reviews.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">●　Do not treat a signed-off aesthetic direction as approval of dimensions or cost.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="BodyLast">Replace illustrative information with verified project records. No approval, legal agreement, or construction readiness is represented. Keep completed client documents in your own secure system.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="PageTwoHeading">Your project</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Project purpose</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Describe the change the project should achieve in one sentence, without naming products too early.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Room and source information</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Record the room reference, dimension source, survey date, and confidence. Nominal dimensions are not site verification.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Functional priorities</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Rank activities and distinguish essential needs from optional additions.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Retained conditions</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">State fixed conditions and what requires condition checks.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Design direction</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Name the agreed concept and explain why it serves the brief. Keep alternatives identifiable.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Deliverables and exclusions</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">List the proposed outputs; refer to a separate scope document for responsibility and limits.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Open decisions</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Record the question, required information, owner, and next review. Unknown is a valid status.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="BodyLast">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="PageThreeHeading">Review record</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Capture the revision, reviewer, date, and what was agreed. A filled example is not actual approval.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="BodyLast">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
    </office:text>
  </office:body>
</office:document>
